{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And when a man strikes.</b> I know only a man — from where [do I derive] a woman? Rabbi Yishmael would say: since it says etc." "<b>With a staff.</b> With an object that people are accustomed to strike a slave with, to discipline him — therefore the bet is open (in the Masoretic text). But if he struck him with a sword, even if he survived a day or two, the master is liable to the death penalty, for this is not discipline but a manner of murder." "<b>And he dies under his hand.</b> In his jurisdiction (lit. permission) — but if he struck him and sold him to another and he died, he is exempt. Another interpretation: <b>and he dies under his hand</b> — at the time of the strike, that he strikes him there until he dies; this is not subjugation but killing with the hands (i.e., intentional murder)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:26.830736387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}